# The plain HTTP server of eAPI, read with `| include ^HTTP server`: one row when it serves
# (running, or starting right after `protocol http`), none when it is shut down or the API is off
# ("enabled"), which the recipe declares empty. Cleartext eAPI is what an audit looks for.
Value STATE (running|starting)
Value PORT (\d+)

Start
  ^HTTP server:\s+${STATE}, set to use port ${PORT}\s*$$ -> Record
  ^HTTP server:\s+(shutdown|enabled),
  ^\s*$$
  ^. -> Error

